Let $f(z)$ be analytic on a domain $D$. If $|f(z)|$ is constant throughout $D$, which statement must hold?

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
$f(z)$ is identically constant in $D$

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
$f(z)$ must vanish at some point in $D$

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
$f'(z)$ is non-zero throughout $D$

#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
$f(z) = e^(i alpha z)$ for some $alpha in RR$

